      "bbox": [
        306,
        185,
        345,
        772
      ],
      "margin_number": 191,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Greek can express the idea of time by the use of case alone:",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 1,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        362,
        233,
        376,
        423
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Accusative (‘throughout’)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        386,
        218,
        419,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The acc. case expresses a length of time, the time throughout which something happens (often expressed in English by ‘for’), e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 2,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        428,
        248,
        467,
        863
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔμενεν ἐν τῇ οἰκίᾳ δέκα ἡμέρας ‘he stayed in the house for 10 days’\nκαθεύδει ὅλην τὴν νύκτα ‘he sleeps (for) the whole night’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 3,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        486,
        233,
        501,
        396
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Genitive (‘within’)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        510,
        218,
        543,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The gen. case expresses time within which something happens (generally expressed in English by ‘during’, ‘in the course of’, ‘within’ or simply ‘in’), e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 4,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        552,
        248,
        607,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τῆς νυκτὸς κρίνει ‘he judges during the night/in (the course of) the night’\nἐπάνειμι δέκα ἡμερῶν ‘I shall return within/in ten days’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 5,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 11,
      "bbox": [
        626,
        233,
        642,
        342
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Dative (‘on’)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 12,
      "bbox": [
        651,
        218,
        683,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "The dat. case expresses the point of time at which something happens (English ‘at, on’), e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": 6,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
